diff --git a/doc/_docstrings/objects.Perc.rst b/doc/_docstrings/objects.Perc.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..109122c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/_docstrings/objects.Perc.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+
+    Parameters
+    ----------
+    k : int or list of float
+        Number of percentile levels to compute, evenly spaced from 0 to 100
+        inclusive, or an explicit list of percentile levels.
+    method : str
+        Method used to calculate the percentile, passed to
+        :func:`numpy.percentile`. The default, ``"linear"``, interpolates
+        between observations. Valid choices are ``"inverted_cdf"``,
+        ``"averaged_inverted_cdf"``, ``"closest_observation"``,
+        ``"interpolated_inverted_cdf"``, ``"hazen"``, ``"weibull"``,
+        ``"linear"``, ``"median_unbiased"``, ``"normal_unbiased"``,
+        ``"lower"``, ``"higher"``, ``"midpoint"``, and ``"nearest"``.
+
+    The statistic returns one row per requested percentile and group. The
+    computed value is stored in the value variable, and the requested level is
+    stored in ``percentile``.
+
+    Examples
+    --------
+    Compute the default quartiles and endpoints:
+
+    .. code:: python
+
+        import seaborn.objects as so
+
+        so.Plot(data, x="group", y="value").add(so.Dot(), so.Perc())
+
+    Request three evenly spaced levels, or specify levels directly:
+
+    .. code:: python
+
+        so.Plot(data, x="group", y="value").add(so.Dot(), so.Perc(3))
+        so.Plot(data, x="group", y="value").add(so.Dot(), so.Perc([10, 50, 90]))
+
+    Combine percentile rows with a range mark to show the interval between
+    selected levels:
+
+    .. code:: python
+
+        so.Plot(data, x="group", y="value").add(so.Range(), so.Perc([10, 90]))
